  "notes": "Post-grunge-lite pop-rock: 63–140 straight with the backbeat on 2&4 and the signature singles at 94–130. Three drum deltas are quoted — \"kick 1 and the '&' of 3\", \"snare 2&4\" with \"a compressed, forward snare\" (the highest main tier in this batch against a moderate accent), and \"8th hat in verse and crash-8ths in the chorus\", which is the crash/ride perc block with a high open-hat probability — plus the fourth stated fact, \"the pre-chorus adds a marching 8th snare\", which is the snare-roll ladder. Harmony is guitar-shape majors with a vi start running vi–IV–I–V and I–V–vi–IV, with \"sus4 suspensions held through the pre-chorus\", so `susSubstitutionProb` is 0.36. The melody is \"in a narrow tenor band with a strained apex on the chorus title\" and the lead is double-tracked with \"harmony only on the final chorus\", which is the narrow register, the arch contour and the low counter ratio. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research says so and marks the harmonic claims **[LOW-CONF]** as convention-based, which is why `keys` is left inherited. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are all drum probabilities and `bpm.mode` 108.",
